{"title":"Career Roadmap · Polymer Engineer","role":"Polymer Engineer","summary":"Career objective: Become a Polymer Engineer capable of designing, processing, testing, modifying, and industrially scaling polymeric materials and products across plastics, rubber, composites, packaging, automotive, electronics, medical devices, construction, and advanced materials.","facts":{},"about":[],"intro":[],"horizons":[],"sections":[{"heading":"Career horizons","kind":"horizons","blocks":[{"type":"table","header":["Stage","Typical focus"],"rows":[[{"text":"2026–2030"},{"text":"B.Tech/B.E. + polymer science + processing + materials testing + internships"}],[{"text":"2030–2033"},{"text":"Polymer/Process/Materials Engineer; develop expertise in a specific polymer technology"}],[{"text":"2033–2038"},{"text":"Senior Polymer Engineer / R&D Engineer / Process Specialist"}],[{"text":"2038–2042"},{"text":"Lead Engineer / Materials Specialist / Technical Manager"}],[{"text":"2042–2046"},{"text":"Principal Polymer Engineer / R&D Manager / Materials Technology Head"}]]}]},{"heading":"What to build during the B.Tech/B.E.","kind":"build","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"Year 1 — Engineering and materials fundamentals"},{"type":"p","text":"Focus on:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Engineering mathematics"},{"text":"Engineering physics and chemistry"},{"text":"Basic thermodynamics"},{"text":"Material science fundamentals"},{"text":"Organic chemistry"},{"text":"Engineering drawing"},{"text":"Basic electrical/mechanical engineering"},{"text":"Programming fundamentals"},{"text":"Technical communication"},{"text":"Excel and engineering data analysis"}]},{"type":"note","label":"Begin building","text":"understanding of polymers versus metals, ceramics, and composites."},{"type":"h","text":"Year 2 — Polymer science foundation"},{"type":"p","text":"Study deeply:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Polymer chemistry"},{"text":"Polymerisation mechanisms"},{"text":"Molecular weight and molecular-weight distribution"},{"text":"Polymer structure and morphology"},{"text":"Thermoplastics"},{"text":"Thermosetting polymers"},{"text":"Elastomers"},{"text":"Additives and fillers"},{"text":"Polymer blends"},{"text":"Polymer composites"},{"text":"Rheology"},{"text":"Polymer thermodynamics"},{"text":"Materials characterisation"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Important polymers to understand:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"PE"},{"text":"PP"},{"text":"PVC"},{"text":"PS"},{"text":"PET"},{"text":"ABS"},{"text":"PA/Nylon"},{"text":"PC"},{"text":"PMMA"},{"text":"POM"},{"text":"PTFE"},{"text":"PU"},{"text":"Epoxy"},{"text":"Silicone"},{"text":"Natural and synthetic rubber"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Year 3 — Polymer processing and industrial engineering"},{"type":"p","text":"This is the core employability stage."},{"type":"p","text":"Master:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Injection moulding"},{"text":"Extrusion"},{"text":"Blow moulding"},{"text":"Compression moulding"},{"text":"Rotational moulding"},{"text":"Thermoforming"},{"text":"Calendering"},{"text":"Film processing"},{"text":"Fibre spinning"},{"text":"Compounding"},{"text":"Polymer recycling"},{"text":"Rheological behaviour"},{"text":"Process optimisation"},{"text":"Mould and die fundamentals"},{"text":"Quality control"},{"text":"Failure analysis"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Learn to understand:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Polymer","formulation","compounding","processing","product","testing","quality","recycling"]},{"type":"p","text":"Useful software/tools:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"CAD"},{"text":"MATLAB/Python"},{"text":"Excel"},{"text":"Minitab or equivalent statistical tools"},{"text":"Basic process simulation"},{"text":"Laboratory characterisation software"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Year 4 — Industrial specialisation"},{"type":"p","text":"Choose one primary direction:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Polymer processing"},{"text":"Polymer R&D"},{"text":"Polymer materials"},{"text":"Plastics manufacturing"},{"text":"Rubber tec